00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.040
The Everyday Zoo!

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.820
Service, service.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.680
Service, service.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.410
Service, service.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.540
Mr. Panda!

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.530
Service, service.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:49.070
Everyone! Let's go see 
Mr. Giraffe next.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.970
Okay!

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.550
This way.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.410
Service, service.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.560
Service, service.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.460
Wow, we worked up quite a sweat.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.040
Thanks, Mr. Full-Time.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.850
What?

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.200
My cuteness is much more noticeable

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.610
when you're around, Mr. Full-Time.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.220
What's wrong?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.060
Oh, it's nothing.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.250
Oh, I know.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.630
Hey, Mr. Full-Time,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.990
let's laze around together.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.880
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.280
It's fun lazing around by myself,

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.490
but it's even more fun lazing 
around together, isn't it?

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.970
You're right.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.700
Next...

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.670
Let's do my side job together.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.870
What? Again?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.980
No way.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.540
When there aren't any visitors, 
 I laze around in private.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.610
Doing a side job together 
is fun, too, Panda.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:22.090
Isn't it more like a chore 
if we do it together?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.490
I'd like to do this with you today.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.370
I'll be right here watching.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.580
When you're doing a side job,

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.060
it only counts when you actually do it.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.020
I told you, no doing side jobs.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.810
Then how am I supposed 
to relieve my boredom?

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.240
Please do your job here.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.960
Come on, Panda, 
let's do this together.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.160
Oh, all right, fine.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.380
Oh? Are you sure, Mr. Handa?

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.540
It's okay?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.600
It is.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.230
Thanks.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.020
Come on, Panda.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.310
Oh, all right.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.630
Please come again.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.730
Mandrill

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.980
Full-Time Panda

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.230
Badger

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.940
Tapir

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.940
Panda

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.940
Anteater

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:15.600
dger

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:15.650
er

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.710
Thanks for all your hard work, Panda.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.450
See you later.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.170
Panda.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:32.540
What?

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.480
No, it's nothing.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:38.660
See you later.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:42.970
See you later.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.170
Yes, see you later.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.740
Miss Sasako,

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.950
could I talk to you about 
something that doesn't matter?

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.930
When someone is saying 
something that doesn't matter,

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.650
should I act like it doesn't matter?

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.420
I don't think you need to ask that.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.180
Miss Sasako,

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.300
you don't really have 
to listen carefully

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.190
when Mr. Penguin is talking in general.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.680
Hey, now!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.100
Isn't talking about things

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.430
that don't matter with your 
good friends the best?

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.390
Indeed.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.790
We'll listen to you talk about 
that don't matter.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.770
This isn't something that needed 
to be discussed that badly.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.500
I'm tired.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.430
I think I'm going to ask to change 
my shift to be once a week, after all.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.230
Would you ask Mr. Handa 
for me, Mr. Penguin?

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:58.660
I can't seem to think 
of a reason I'd ask.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.500
Can you think of one, Polar Bear?

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.700
It's also the best to listen

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.760
to impossible demands from 
your good friends, too.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.970
Well, yeah, that is the best...

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.770
Oh, all right. 
I'll have Mr. Full-Time Panda ask.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.120
Could I get my usual, Miss Sasako?

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:17.760
Sure.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.620
Tapir

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.620
Mandrill

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.620
Badger

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.620
Panda

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.620
Anteater

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:44.890
Huh?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.260
I wonder if Mr. Full-Time 
Panda is late today.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.310
Jeez.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.940
I guess I'll help out since I'm bored.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:09.480
Oh, Mr. Handa. 
Where's Mr. Full-Time?

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.200
Is he late?

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.070
Um...

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:17.600
Mr. Handa...

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.000
Mr. Full-Time Panda 
went to Singapore.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.210
Singapore?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.210
Yeah, it's another country.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:33.240
When's he coming back?

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:34.890
Well...

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.690
he got transferred overseas.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.100
He won't be coming back to this zoo.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.180
Huh?

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.280
This is from Mr. Full-Time Panda.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.700
To Panda
 
Full-Time Panda

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.380
The transfer order 
came in a while back,

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.420
but he asked us not to tell you.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.050
But without Mr. Full-Time Panda here,

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.700
my cuteness won't be as noticeable.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:22.890
So cute!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:23.650
He's cute!

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.790
Oh my!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:25.990
Amazing!

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.020
Isn't that cute?

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.680
How's Panda doing?

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.620
He seems the same as usual.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.610
I see, that's good.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:54.300
All right, see you again tomorrow.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.700
I wonder if Panda will be okay.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.770
<i>Dear Panda,</i>

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.540
<i>I'm sorry I left without 
saying anything.</i>

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:27.690
<i>My transfer came out of nowhere,</i>

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:32.020
<i>and I've been reassigned 
to a zoo in Singapore.</i>

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:39.110
<i>I personally asked Mr. Handa and 
the others not to tell you.</i>

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.770
<i>I was being selfish.</i>

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:46.230
<i>So, please, don't be angry at them.</i>

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.200
<i>I wanted to spend our 
last days together having</i>

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.280
<i>fun like we always did.</i>

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.980
<i>I only saw you twice a week,</i>

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.890
<i>but I had a lot of fun with 
you being there, Panda.</i>

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.160
<i>Also, I'm sure it's 
hot in Singapore,</i>

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.620
<i>so I'm going to leave the kotatsu.</i>

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.210
<i>Feel free to use it.</i>

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.770
<i>Also, I'll leave behind 
the supplies for my side job</i>

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.000
<i>so you can do it if you get bored.</i>

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:26.180
<i>I wish we could have made even 
more visitors happy together.</i>

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.220
<i>Thank you, Panda.</i>

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:32.460
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:37.830
Please take one.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.580
Please take one.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:40.970
Please take one.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.240
Please take one.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.710
Internet Café

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:51.630
<i>Panda...</i>

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.460
<i>Doing a side job together is fun, too.</i>

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:02.580
Oh, I'm sorry. 
Did you not want one?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.530
Without Mr. Full-Time here, I...

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.200
Huh?

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.360
Mr. Full-Time...

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.830
U-Um...

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.210
Um...

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.090
Are you all right?

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.400
Man, when you're a penguin,

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.030
it's hard to find a place 
to put your change.

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.230
Mr. Penguin.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:57.940
What?

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.060
What's wrong with Panda?

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.970
Let's leave him alone for a while.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:14.240
Huh?

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.030
The Zoo in the Rain.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.530
So, how's Panda doing?

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.000
I heard he's not doing too well.

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:52.500
The whole thing with Mr. Full-Time 
Panda happened so suddenly.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:59.740
The thing I wanted to talk 
to you about today...

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:06.320
You know, Mr. Full-Time 
Panda transferred...

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.100
Yeah...

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:16.850
So right now at our zoo, 
you're our only panda, right?

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:18.810
Yeah.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:23.260
And you only work twice a week, right?

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:28.570
So visitors are only able to see 
a panda twice a week at our zoo.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.170
So, this is only if you can,

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.650
but it'd help us out a lot if you 
could work like five days a week

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.500
until we find another part-time panda.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.680
Oh, three days a week is fine, as well.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.390
I guess Mr. Full-Time 
isn't here anymore, huh?

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.810
Mr. Panda!

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:06.140
I wonder what got into Panda?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:10.950
I never thought he'd say he'd 
like to work seven days a week.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.520
But that does help out a lot.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:16.770
But...

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.400
we really need to find 
another part-timer soon.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.130
What?!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.290
Seven days a week?!

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.090
Yes.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.230
By seven days a week...

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.790
You do mean <i>that</i> seven 
days a week, right?

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.020
Everyone is surprised.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:39.480
The same Panda who worked twice a week
 and wanted to only work once a week?

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:44.110
It seems Mr. Handa did say
 three days a week would work...

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.900
The same Panda who wanted to show up
 in the afternoon on his two days a week?

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:52.780
He hasn't really been 
around here lately, either.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.340
He seems to be rather busy...

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.620
What's the deal with Panda?

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.990
I wonder if he doesn't understand 
the calendar anymore.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.850
I don't think that's quite it.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.230
Could I get another, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.000
Sure.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.250
Good morning, Panda.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.650
Good morning, Mr. Llama.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:32.180
Panda's keeping up pretty well.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:35.230
He hasn't had a day off so far.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:39.290
Cute!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:41.920
Super cute!

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:54.780
Mr. Handa, could you 
pinch me on the cheek?

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.390
Cute.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:55.390
Huh?

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:59.970
I can't seem to believe that Panda 
is actually working every day.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:03.460
And we should get back 
to work, as well.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.790
R-Right.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:06.740
Mr. Panda!

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:16.060
Here's your coffee.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:17.790
Thank you very much.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.240
I heard that Panda's 
working very hard.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.820
Indeed. Seven days a week 
must be rather hard.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:28.990
Out of all the jobs at the zoo, 
his is one of the busiest.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:30.780
You're right.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.710
I wonder if Panda is doing all right.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.380
It's already been two weeks.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.770
Hey, everyone's so worried,

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.620
but it's normal to work 
every day, isn't it?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.570
I think all of you are 
spoiling Panda too much.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.480
You think so?

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.640
He's so tired that he's asleep.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.300
Well, it's been two weeks.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.080
You're right.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:15.510
By the way, Mr. Handa.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.790
There are still quite a

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:21.400
few visitors on Valentine's 
Day, despite this rain.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.370
Especially couples.

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.690
That's enough. 
Come on, back to work.

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:28.740
Did you get any chocola—

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.770
I said work!

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.860
Right.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.810
Here's the panda!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:36.610
Come on!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.150
Oh, all right.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:52.100
He's like asleep and won't move.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.910
What the hell's up with that panda?

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.270
This sucks. Let's go.

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:00.730
Yeah.

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:03.010
What do you mean, "this sucks"?

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:07.190
What do you mean, "this sucks"?!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:13.990
It's true that Panda is usually a lazy 
guy who only works twice a week!

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:15.530
Wh-What the hell?

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.870
Panda...

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:22.660
always tried to get his shift covered 
if the littlest thing happened!

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.870
He'd laze around and not work,

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.400
he hated the rush hour 
train in the morning,

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.790
and he always, constantly, 
thought about how to skip out on work.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.250
He hates working,

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:37.860
and he likes to just 
lay around the Café!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.680
He's seriously a total loser!

00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:47.640
But do you even know how hard 
that Panda is working?!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.700
Do you?!

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.470
Don't you dare say this sucks!

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.390
What's his problem?

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:01.420
I'm Panda's best friend!

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:06.270
Hey, let's go.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:07.160
Y-Yeah.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:03.260
I see. So they found a 
new part-time panda?

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:04.620
Yeah.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:09.800
I totally feel alive again after 
going back to two days a week.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.540
Here you go, Panda. Have this.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.380
What?

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:18.440
I didn't order this.

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:20.810
It's on the house.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:28.580
Oh, Mr. Penguin.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.230
Hey, Panda. You're here.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.040
I heard from Mr. Handa...

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:43.690
That you were ranting 
at the zoo the other day.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.880
Everyday stress?

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:49.430
F-For your sake, I...

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.230
Oh, whatever.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:01.040
Here.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.790
I didn't order this.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.700
It's on the house.

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.000
Really? Thanks!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:19.710
It's delicious, isn't it, Mr. Penguin?

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:22.750
Yeah.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.390
Hey, Mr. Penguin.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:26.680
What is it?

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:31.430
It's been a while, so tell me all sorts 
of things that don't matter.

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:34.810
I'd rather not when you 
put it that way...

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.690
All right, I will.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.020
Oh, I know.

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.860
Um... you're just going 
to ignore me now?

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:46.930
Mr. Penguin, look at this.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:48.320
What?

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:52.050
Look! I got a postcard.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.710
From Mr. Full-Time Panda?

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:55.840
Yeah!

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:01.460
Apparently there are side 
jobs in Singapore, too!

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:02.710
Wow.

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:05.810
Mr. Full-Time Panda seems 
to be doing well.

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:09.890
He said he'd keep sending 
postcards from time to time.

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:15.780
Good for you, Panda.

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:17.030
Yeah!

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:25.560
Next Time

00:23:58.270 --> 00:23:59.790
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.090
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:04.210
Please scold the people 
who don't say a word

00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:06.670
while they are eating crab!

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:09.270
I don't know why that'd 
call for a scolding,

00:24:09.270 --> 00:24:10.660
but don't use the crab as an excuse!

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:12.110
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:12.110 --> 00:24:14.050
You totally just wanted to 
say that, didn't you?

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.810
I'm sorry, I just wanted to try it.

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:17.490
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:19.210
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:21.770
will be brought to you with even 
more alpha waves than normal.

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:21.770
Alpha 
waves

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:23.320
We don't emit them to begin with.

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:24.360
Rin Rin and Mei Mei's 
Super Exciting Plan
Smelt Fishing

00:24:23.320 --> 00:24:24.360
Enjoy!
